## 4. austrophile-mcp — plan

### 4.1 Product one-liner

Local-first **Austria + German (AT)** workstation: ÖSD-oriented drills, Austrian culture Knowledge box, Vienna-centric Travel crossconnects, diary/progress.

### 4.2 MCP tools (five portmanteaus, names TBD)

| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `{austro}_help` | Ports, DB paths, knowledge count, fetch hints |
| `german_*` or `de_*` | Lookup/search vocabulary, grammar tags, CEFR/ÖSD level filters |
| `exam_*` | ÖSD / Goethe-shaped mock items (seed MCQ); prefer “exam” in UI not unexplained acronyms |
| `vocab_*` | Phrase search against seed + optional big corpus |
| `knowledge_*` | list/get HTML culture pages |

No kanji wall — replace with **vocabulary + case/gender drills** in Practice.

### 4.3 Language curriculum tabs (HTML under `assets/language/`)

| Tab | Content focus |
|-----|----------------|
| Overview | DE in Austria vs DE in Germany; Sie/du; Austrian lexical shibboleths (Jänner, Paradeiser, …) |
| Writing | ß/ss, capitalization, umlaut input; no hanzi — **compound nouns** and spelling reform notes |
| Grammar | Cases, verb position, separable verbs, Konjunktiv II polite |
| Phonetics | Regional vowels (Viennese), stress; contrast High German vs local color |
| Vocabulary | Educated lexicon scale; Austrianisms; false friends with English |
| Materials | **Calibre-Bibliothek Deutsch** + pocket vs course books; Goethe/ÖSD/Hueber; jisui/ebook gap |
| Mobile | iPhone/iPad: DW, Anki, Der Die Das, ÖSD apps |
| Exams | ÖSD levels, Goethe equivalence, limits (which skills tested) |
| Bloopers | Common L1 English errors; **Ohrwurm** vs embarrassing false friends; Servus misuse |

Optional tab: **Kaffeehaus & Alltag** (culture register, not grammar).

### 4.4 Knowledge clusters

History (Habsburg to EU), Bundesländer, politics/economy (neutral), daily life, food (Sachertorte vs tourist traps), music (Klassik, Schlager, Austropop), travel (Wien, Salzkammergut, …), crime/society (Fritzl-level topics handled carefully), sport.

### 4.5 Plan face

Phase 1: static Travel page + deep links to **mywienerlinien** webapp and gtfs-mcp tools.  
Phase 2: itinerary MCP tools (reuse patterns from japanophile Stage 4 PRD).

### 4.6 Data seeds

- ÖSD/CEFR vocabulary seed (JSON/SQLite)  
- 500–800 MCQ grammar/vocab items  
- 25–40 knowledge HTML pages (vendored or authored)  
- Optional: hook **directmedia-mcp** for DigiBib German references (crosslink only)

### 4.7 Scaffold checklist

1. `git init` + initial commit per [GIT_REPOSITORY_SAFETY.md](../standards/GIT_REPOSITORY_SAFETY.md)  
2. Fork japanophile tree: rename package, strip JLPT/kanji, insert DE tools  
3. Register ports **11195/11196**  
4. MCD: `projects/austrophile-mcp/` (README, STATUS, PHILE copy of INSTALL)  
5. Skill: `skills/austria-expert/SKILL.md`  
6. Pilot: `uv run pytest`, `just check`, one NSIS smoke (Stage 3 parity when stable)

### 4.8 vienna-living (contributor repo)

**vienna-living** is a **weak contributor** — not the canonical home for Austrian culture curriculum (that is **austrophile-mcp**), but a source of lived Vienna content:

| Role | Owner |
|------|--------|
| Practical daily life (Bezirke, Amt, Müll, Kinder, doctors) | vienna-living |
| Language curriculum + ÖSD tooling + Knowledge HTML box | austrophile-mcp |
| Transit deep links | mywienerlinien / gtfs-mcp |

**Integration pattern:** vendoring or git submodule snippets into `assets/knowledge/austria/` with attribution; austrophile **Travel / Daily life** clusters link out to vienna-living pages where they exist. Do not duplicate — **crosslink + short excerpt**. Register vienna-living in fleet-registry when repo path is stable under `D:/Dev/repos/vienna-living`.

