## 5. sinophile-mcp — plan

### 5.1 Product one-liner

Local-first **Chinese language + civilization** workstation: hanzi tools (simp/trad), HSK-oriented exams, tone-aware curriculum, Knowledge box, travel planner, diary.

### 5.2 MCP tools (five portmanteaus)

| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `{sino}_help` | Status, paths, fetch hints |
| `hanzi_*` | Lookup by character, radical, stroke count, level tag (HSK 1–6) |
| `exam_*` | HSK-style reading/grammar MCQ from seed bank |
| `vocab_*` | Pinyin search, English gloss, measure word where applicable |
| `knowledge_*` | Culture/history HTML |

### 5.3 Language curriculum tabs

| Tab | Content focus |
|-----|----------------|
| Overview | Mandarin vs Cantonese note; simp/trad; pinyin as default romanization (not Wade-Giles except historical) |
| Writing | Simplified/traditional toggle mindset; radicals; stroke order; **Script reform FAQ** (why Mao pushed 简化字 + 拼音 but not full latinization — homophony, dialects, literacy politics, Taiwan split; founder note: interesting even if you never study Chinese) |
| Grammar | 了 le aspect, 把 ba, classifiers 个/本/…, topic-comment |
| Phonetics | **Four tones + neutral**; sandhi (不, 一); why English speakers fail tones |
| Vocabulary | Educated lexicon (~5k HSK6 floor vs 30k+ literary); measure words |
| Materials | HSK Standard Course, New Practical Chinese Reader, **Calibre** (add **Calibre-Bibliothek Chinesisch** or tag `language-learning` + `chinese`); Pleco; jisui |
| Mobile | Pleco, Skritter, HelloChinese, Du Chinese, HSK apps |
| Exams | HSK 3.0 bands, TOCFL (Taiwan), what is not tested (speaking in standard HSK computer test) |
| Bloopers | Tone pairs (mā/má/mǎ/mà); 是 shì vs 十 shí; polite vs direct; 面子 |

Culture-specific: **Honorfics / address** tab (先生, 您) lighter than Japanese keigo.

### 5.4 Knowledge clusters

Dynasties timeline, cuisine regional map, philosophy intro, travel, literature (public domain), contemporary society.

**Politics / modern history cluster — gated:** ships only after [EDITORIAL_CHARTER.md](./sinophile-mcp/EDITORIAL_CHARTER.md) sign-off. Includes PRC/post-1949 (sourced, dated), diaspora, Hong Kong/Macau notes, and **Taiwan** as flagship ([TAIWAN_KNOWLEDGE_OUTLINE.md](./sinophile-mcp/TAIWAN_KNOWLEDGE_OUTLINE.md)).

Reject **sinophobe US cottage industry** and **CCP united-front** voice equally in our HTML — see charter.

### 5.5 Data seeds

- Hanzi seed (HSK 1–6 character list + definitions)  
- HSK vocabulary SQLite (compact)  
- MCQ seed bank (reading/grammar)  
- CC-CEDICT or equivalent **fetched** (large)  
- Knowledge HTML pack (translate/adapt japanophile pipeline)

### 5.6 Practice games

Port or author: tone trainer, radical drill, HSK vocab quiz, optional character writing grid. Keep heavy arcade out.

### 5.7 Scaffold checklist

Same as §4.7 with ports **11197/11198**, package `sinophile_mcp`, skill `sinophile-expert`, Calibre library split TBD.

### 5.8 Editorial finesse (non-optional)

Owner is **very sinophile** (language, culture, food, history) — enthusiasm in Language and benign Knowledge. **Politics/history** = slow, cited, multi-perspective; skill refuses agitprop.

Taiwan article mandatory before other hot takes: indigenous peoples, Han colonization, pirate/backwater centuries, Japanese era, KMT violent early rule then democratization, cross-strait economic entanglement, **TSMC**, domestic parties — and explicit rejection of **"war with China over Taiwan"** war-fever (foreign policy theatre that skips island history). Neither DPP-as-cartoon-villain nor "renegade province" boilerplate as article voice.

Human review on Tier-A pages (Taiwan first; Tibet/Xinjiang-class only if ever added with same bar).

### 5.9 Taiwan flagship (summary)

Full section brief: [TAIWAN_KNOWLEDGE_OUTLINE.md](./sinophile-mcp/TAIWAN_KNOWLEDGE_OUTLINE.md). Phase **P4b** before politics cluster goes public.

